#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161693 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162127 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56c44f33-e6d3-5e34-9d9d-ded24576b82e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Conditional Expectations Given Joint and Marginal PDFs"}] :question/id #uuid "2eda20ae-ff4f-5c78-abaa-2c176968e908" :question/math-academy-id "e-10311" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y-x, & -1\\le x\\le 0,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}+y, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\textrm{E}\\bigg[X \\,\\bigg|\\, Y=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\bigg].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm E\\big[ X \\,|\\, Y = y \\big] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x \\, f_{X|Y}(x \\,|\\, y) \\; \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\textrm E\\big[ X \\,|\\, Y = y \\big]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{y-x}{\\frac{1}{2}+y} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(y-x)}{1+2y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $-1 \\leq x \\leq 0, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1.$ Outside this domain, we have $f_{X|Y} (x \\,|\\, y) = 0.$\n\nNow, substituting $y=\\dfrac{1}{2}$ into the expression for $f_{X|Y} (x \\,|\\, y),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{2(\\frac{1}{2}-x)}{1+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-2x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{2}] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}x(\\frac{1}{2}-x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(\\frac{x}{2}-{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =0-(\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161694 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162128 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea596df6-f52e-5347-afdd-78521b40525e" :knowledge-point/title "Conditional Expectation as a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "3de4a4e5-824f-504b-ad7c-f088dd7569fd" :question/math-academy-id "e-10315" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+y}{4}, & 0\\le y\\le x,\\,\\,0<x<2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8}, & 0<x<2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\textrm{E}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=x\\big]$ for $0 <     x <     2.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm E\\big[ Y \\,|\\, X = x \\big] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y \\, f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, x) \\; \\textrm{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\textrm E\\big[ Y \\,|\\, X = x \\big]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{x+y}{4})}{(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+y)}{3{x}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0 \\leq y \\leq x,\\; 0 <              x <             2.$ Outside this domain, we have $f_{Y|X} (y \\,|\\, x) = 0.$ \n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}y\\cdot \\,\\frac{2(x+y)}{3{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{x}(xy+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3{x}^{2}}{[\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3{x}^{2}}[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{5{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{5{x}^{2}\\cdot x}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cancel{{x}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{5\\cancel{{x}^{2}}\\cdot x}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5x}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161695 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162129 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcf85ec6-b20d-5540-a709-9ff28bc82ca6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation From a Conditional PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "52bad65a-5481-5529-8e25-2763f57b755a" :question/math-academy-id "e-10316" :question/problem "![](images/e5/e5f658b08e954097ef9ed39ebb935e800251a2ef729a02bc18240a0ca89167cc.svg) \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. Find the conditional expected value $\\textrm{E}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=1\\big]$ given that the conditional probability density function $f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, 1)$ is shown above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm E\\big[ Y \\,|\\, X = x \\big] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y \\, f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, x) \\; \\textrm{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{3(1+{y}^{2})}{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y+{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162129 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcf85ec6-b20d-5540-a709-9ff28bc82ca6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation From a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "983d667f-9351-5c43-8159-d56fc2c1baf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159705} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a66dcc-b0e1-5c5f-8805-7ece90dd1f9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159706} {:answer/id #uuid "ba66cfd7-6641-5691-ac4e-8e5020696fdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159707} {:answer/id #uuid "c866d6c5-1212-580c-bdd7-2206d8fe3fab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159708} {:answer/id #uuid "6e5c21d5-588f-537b-ba3e-55ecf0a0ce93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c866d6c5-1212-580c-bdd7-2206d8fe3fab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159708} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e99ef04-2d76-564c-b8d0-1708478bdb2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e557597-cc36-56e6-a5ea-6609d5dea4e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-145631" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{4}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 3 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=2]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ is shown above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=2] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\cdot \\frac{x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{12}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{12}-\\frac{1}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520489 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162129 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcf85ec6-b20d-5540-a709-9ff28bc82ca6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation From a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24f3a31a-ee9a-521d-b968-a205010ab955" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520045} {:answer/id #uuid "5619230d-a436-5ed6-8a1e-b2a127ca19a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520126} {:answer/id #uuid "77133d69-998c-59fb-b57b-d052bbea19f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520164} {:answer/id #uuid "abc22133-fdf5-57dd-8c1c-1501423e681c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520227} {:answer/id #uuid "c676628d-a2e3-5f46-80cd-2839d9b7b1b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77133d69-998c-59fb-b57b-d052bbea19f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520164} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1e39338-61c3-579d-a5f3-089f42737d5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a3d747d1-36eb-5ac7-aecf-ff0858227dfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-146177" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,3)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8}, & \\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=3]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3)$ is shown above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=3] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{32}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{32}-\\frac{0}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520503 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162129 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcf85ec6-b20d-5540-a709-9ff28bc82ca6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation From a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "136bf4b6-26e2-5491-9a45-4dc0a744ce96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520016} {:answer/id #uuid "48b03958-5e31-5aeb-a187-15ffa3fb9dfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520101} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d48e89-2b69-5bc2-931c-f7aff7dddcd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520219} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a68f91-be81-5c57-9644-bf8d7a859773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520244} {:answer/id #uuid "c61dfa67-f506-5960-a9d7-adb05ec9f915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "136bf4b6-26e2-5491-9a45-4dc0a744ce96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520016} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f03a1d0-67c6-5c08-a36d-a749c3ea0785" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "db6164d4-0ab9-5b8d-a944-50886d9aea3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-146180" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+{y}^{2}}{12}, & \\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ is shown above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\cdot \\frac{1+{y}^{2}}{12}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(y+{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{48}(99-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520458 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162129 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcf85ec6-b20d-5540-a709-9ff28bc82ca6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation From a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1813320d-4887-55b9-9dad-afa95a010f45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520027} {:answer/id #uuid "3e481426-5239-5f6c-8193-9deaaf8eef05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520082} {:answer/id #uuid "4dd2746a-eb77-58a0-8586-c29564895209" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520110} {:answer/id #uuid "63999174-c937-5b70-8f31-1c0a52497413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520144} {:answer/id #uuid "db0f44e2-0364-5450-843f-ba45ebf9b0a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e481426-5239-5f6c-8193-9deaaf8eef05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520082} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1557da6-b2bd-5567-b11c-16c8afd17b98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "33de5000-925c-5b02-ae4e-01b5310d9ba9" :question/math-academy-id "q-146188" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2+2y}{3}, & \\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ is shown above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{2+2y}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520449 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162129 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcf85ec6-b20d-5540-a709-9ff28bc82ca6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation From a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03237e50-d501-53e6-bba6-d412fef03733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519999} {:answer/id #uuid "15d71dd1-c21c-5526-a084-8500b3aafe65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520021} {:answer/id #uuid "55acfb92-edbe-511d-ae97-c980cd7635ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520125} {:answer/id #uuid "675b9382-7ebc-5320-991c-3b7b3054e588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520149} {:answer/id #uuid "acb66d99-3833-5c6b-8869-35f24a432fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acb66d99-3833-5c6b-8869-35f24a432fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520229} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc4a1905-341f-5668-92f7-b536136635df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520427}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0729c3e7-6c49-5561-ba72-ac80cc555328" :question/math-academy-id "q-146238" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,1.5)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(1+2{y}^{2})}{5}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1.5]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1.5)$ is shown above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1.5] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1.5)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{3(1+2{y}^{2})}{5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y+2{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520491 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162127 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56c44f33-e6d3-5e34-9d9d-ded24576b82e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Conditional Expectations Given Joint and Marginal PDFs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d6fd54d-4c1c-55c6-8760-81621dbc6cde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520007} {:answer/id #uuid "1ddc283e-0948-540b-b84c-d2835daf8f6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520035} {:answer/id #uuid "416e4a5c-22d6-5be2-bec7-c3eae49ba017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520084} {:answer/id #uuid "4661b057-e34b-5ad1-86ad-f2170ff87ca2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520095} {:answer/id #uuid "ef193c69-7a43-5081-98b8-a77c6b8cc73b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4661b057-e34b-5ad1-86ad-f2170ff87ca2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520095} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce1f1101-3df3-5c9e-9c08-818c39307178" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b25c780b-4145-5bfa-8e04-0856e9d67d3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-146253" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+3y}{12}, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y+1}{4}, & 0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2x+3y}{12})}{(\\frac{y+1}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+3y}{3y+3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $y=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{2x+3\\cdot 1}{3\\cdot 1+3}=\\frac{2x+3}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{2x+3}{6}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(2{x}^{2}+3x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}((\\frac{16}{3}+6)-(\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{3}{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{55}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520463 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162127 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56c44f33-e6d3-5e34-9d9d-ded24576b82e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Conditional Expectations Given Joint and Marginal PDFs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a683496-0c43-5971-b86f-6d13331e35b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520028} {:answer/id #uuid "3307e64e-4740-5753-a998-4d2bb44bacd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520066} {:answer/id #uuid "b0cc6f69-e221-5d61-9deb-81c1dda05489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520234} {:answer/id #uuid "b1c5dbb7-48c6-5964-a81c-58dd2ea3eb31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520236} {:answer/id #uuid "daf6bfcb-1f9b-5de5-bb85-1dda5505c8a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a683496-0c43-5971-b86f-6d13331e35b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520028} :answer-field/id #uuid "8527a0b3-bf88-546e-9eb5-59cbca7c2a30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4aa42e03-e8d1-5333-8d07-d9074e34a91f" :question/math-academy-id "q-146254" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2-x-y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}-y, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2-x-y)}{(\\frac{3}{2}-y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-2x-2y}{3-2y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $y=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{4-2x-2\\cdot 1}{3-2\\cdot 1}=\\frac{4-2x-2}{3-2}=2-2x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(2-2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2x-2{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(1-\\frac{2}{3})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520451 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162127 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56c44f33-e6d3-5e34-9d9d-ded24576b82e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Conditional Expectations Given Joint and Marginal PDFs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b420ea0-e242-5852-9a3b-163544334e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520075} {:answer/id #uuid "4d1c5347-c759-549b-a191-bc31ec802b90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520109} {:answer/id #uuid "dedd649a-149f-5255-a5fc-3c20f9338e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520314} {:answer/id #uuid "e6bfe5a6-d3b1-5081-ab2c-efd0c7a6f4b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520328} {:answer/id #uuid "fbc01020-4089-56e6-82f5-6c8e9efb10f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dedd649a-149f-5255-a5fc-3c20f9338e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520314} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec37af3f-2077-53c3-aed3-459ba8fcb5e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13aa670b-3e27-50cc-b24b-f562a4443719" :question/math-academy-id "q-146337" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(x+{y}^{2})}{8}, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x+1}{8}, & 0\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3x+{y}^{2}}{8})}{(\\frac{3x+1}{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(x+{y}^{2})}{3x+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $x=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{3(1+{y}^{2})}{3\\cdot 1+1}=\\frac{3(1+{y}^{2})}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{3(1+{y}^{2})}{4}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y+{y}^{3})\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{4})-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162127 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56c44f33-e6d3-5e34-9d9d-ded24576b82e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Conditional Expectations Given Joint and Marginal PDFs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "432f54a1-0935-5f8b-8bdb-b406503cc001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520087} {:answer/id #uuid "45744fcc-0b9f-52ee-b902-f9e64f031117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520093} {:answer/id #uuid "816c831b-ddb4-5f28-8334-ebe8e11c9a11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520179} {:answer/id #uuid "d716ab8f-83c1-5df4-9c34-94965f151237" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520293} {:answer/id #uuid "fad6c54a-1f9e-59a7-8d04-ec373071feac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "816c831b-ddb4-5f28-8334-ebe8e11c9a11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520179} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b646b3b-c884-5b9e-bf55-39ae165ad7cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520403}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "28a2968a-07fa-5df6-a93c-3d505caa4a83" :question/math-academy-id "q-146345" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}12xy, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{5}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{12xy}{6{x}^{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{{x}^{4}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $0<x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $x=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|1\\,)=2y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot (2y)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{y}^{2})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520492 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162127 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56c44f33-e6d3-5e34-9d9d-ded24576b82e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Conditional Expectations Given Joint and Marginal PDFs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "626e204c-7f48-5f37-9d37-b43ff67dd7df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520143} {:answer/id #uuid "7fefcb29-5c38-5744-a9ee-086455686bd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520174} {:answer/id #uuid "8220d898-eba8-5608-acb9-26ef0ebbb5ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520180} {:answer/id #uuid "9246a3b3-e505-5724-80de-0b473089adf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520201} {:answer/id #uuid "f88a890a-b584-5141-85df-189f2967c419" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8220d898-eba8-5608-acb9-26ef0ebbb5ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520180} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd3b5bb7-8ff5-583c-95ec-4d9a61d8d3e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b86ab1d5-8833-598a-9757-b29ccf7f9acc" :question/math-academy-id "q-146360" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}8xy, & 0<x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le x, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}, & 0<x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8xy}{4{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $0<x\\le 1,\\,0<y\\le x.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$    \n\nNow, substituting $x=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|1\\,)=2y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot (2y)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{y}^{2})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520474 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162128 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea596df6-f52e-5347-afdd-78521b40525e" :knowledge-point/title "Conditional Expectation as a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b7b8be0-cd7d-5f2a-8d07-58b09b3e02bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520106} {:answer/id #uuid "51d6868e-9f63-566b-8657-3e46a79dcf7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520115} {:answer/id #uuid "a358ba73-65d0-5ebe-ae65-bacd7eb25e86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520216} {:answer/id #uuid "a6fae95c-8607-5baf-bcfe-438d0e382039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520220} {:answer/id #uuid "cf07accb-49d6-5bf1-b6e5-cfad1ed38be2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51d6868e-9f63-566b-8657-3e46a79dcf7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520115} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a063c31-7ea1-511c-9093-dca00ca75be6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7abac60c-426c-5228-9bff-bdb217864577" :question/math-academy-id "q-146397" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x{y}^{2}}{4}, & 0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ for $0<x<1.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3x{y}^{2}}{4})}{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{8},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0<x<1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$ \n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\cdot \\,\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{8}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}[4-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162128 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea596df6-f52e-5347-afdd-78521b40525e" :knowledge-point/title "Conditional Expectation as a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2264b36a-087e-594e-9217-a261fcae3477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520041} {:answer/id #uuid "3d8d2dd6-e5cd-5281-b1e3-60c2038d557b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520077} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7eaf44-8b6d-58de-8df7-7db229ea766f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520150} {:answer/id #uuid "90b18d84-cb8b-5c38-81d9-e6a9d91dbc74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520200} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec52a3e-3a84-504f-a2f1-f568cc685635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ec52a3e-3a84-504f-a2f1-f568cc685635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520211} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fa98042-2de8-53a0-9725-b83197c63351" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520416}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4a9126d5-9f56-54dd-b358-d393eac16b93" :question/math-academy-id "q-146433" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}, & 0\\le y\\le 4,\\,0<x<\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}24{x}^{2}, & 0<x<\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ for $0<x<\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{x}^{2}}{24{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le y\\le 4,\\,0<x<\\frac{1}{2}.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$ \n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}y\\cdot \\,\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\frac{16}{2}-0] \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520452 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162128 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea596df6-f52e-5347-afdd-78521b40525e" :knowledge-point/title "Conditional Expectation as a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49e3ff31-b227-5b2a-8fe3-d34a74248ace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520103} {:answer/id #uuid "8262ba09-25dc-5226-a050-4bcaa05979b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+y}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520182} {:answer/id #uuid "b9ece17e-ce07-5a63-9272-3986c9fc0b28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520253} {:answer/id #uuid "da064ca0-ec2d-5668-b781-affcc343f33c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+y}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520299} {:answer/id #uuid "fa62812a-5ad0-5c54-8abe-7a6dfef958dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23x}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa62812a-5ad0-5c54-8abe-7a6dfef958dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23x}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520358} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f740bd4-a687-5983-91a3-7513fe971934" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "200b9c27-2539-5e86-b17a-fa5314a06310" :question/math-academy-id "q-146517" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6(x+y)}{5}, & x\\le y\\le 2x,\\,0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ for $0<x<1.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{6(x+y)}{5})}{3{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+y)}{5{x}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x\\le y\\le 2x,\\,0<x<1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{x}^{2x}y\\cdot \\,\\frac{2(x+y)}{5{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{x}^{2x}(xy+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5{x}^{2}}{[\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{x}^{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5{x}^{2}}[(\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{3})-(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{23{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cancel{{x}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{23x\\cdot \\cancel{({x}^{2})}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{23x}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520464 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162128 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea596df6-f52e-5347-afdd-78521b40525e" :knowledge-point/title "Conditional Expectation as a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ccc6750-246a-5a6e-8d0b-5e04b2fcec20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(1+2y)}{4(3y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520032} {:answer/id #uuid "445f339a-c1d1-5908-9ed9-b51956b4aff3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(1+2y)}{4(3y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520089} {:answer/id #uuid "73ea5849-0a8b-5581-9a68-493551edf6c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(1+2y)}{(3y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520159} {:answer/id #uuid "8bf1aa4b-de93-56ed-90a9-5e53ffe6181a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y}{2(3y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520196} {:answer/id #uuid "c6a557fd-77df-511c-836c-c00052e9bf42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{4(y+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "445f339a-c1d1-5908-9ed9-b51956b4aff3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(1+2y)}{4(3y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520089} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d5798b6-1edf-5ed2-bbb7-aae35b6bf653" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c1f6156-411f-54e4-bb68-bbf84af25120" :question/math-academy-id "q-146520" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6{x}^{2}+6y}{5}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0<y<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6y+2}{5}, & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ for $0<y<1.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{6{x}^{2}+6y}{5})}{(\\frac{6y+2}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{x}^{2}+6y}{6y+2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$ \n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\,\\frac{6{x}^{2}+6y}{6y+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{6y+2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}+xy)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{6y+2}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{6y+2}[\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{y}{2}-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{6y+2}\\cdot \\frac{1+2y}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2(3y+1)}\\cdot \\frac{(1+2y)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1+2y)}{4(3y+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520466 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162128 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea596df6-f52e-5347-afdd-78521b40525e" :knowledge-point/title "Conditional Expectation as a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bf9c026-9fde-556b-a693-fbda3046a227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(1+4y)}{(1+3y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520030} {:answer/id #uuid "46d79442-5892-5af0-818d-d2ead962340e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(y+3)}{3(y+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520098} {:answer/id #uuid "5345dbd5-7e99-5317-8490-c789146a8788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(1+3y)}{(1+4y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520116} {:answer/id #uuid "db470a65-0a51-550a-8ffd-cf65f10f85a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(1+3y)}{3(1+4y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520305} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e56427-f6a7-5af0-99d9-80933b07e001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(1+3y)}{3(1+4y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db470a65-0a51-550a-8ffd-cf65f10f85a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(1+3y)}{3(1+4y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520305} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1a039c4-3510-5a92-9df7-feb0d8d5d857" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5142c769-0ab4-5c62-90f2-d5f937ec0c66" :question/math-academy-id "q-146538" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(x+2y)}{3}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+4y}{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ for $0\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2(x+2y)}{3})}{(\\frac{1+4y}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+2y)}{1+4y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$ \n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\,\\frac{2(x+2y)}{1+4y}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+4y}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+2yx)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+4y}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+y{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+4y}\\cdot [\\frac{1}{3}+y-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+4y}\\cdot \\frac{1+3y}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1+3y)}{3(1+4y)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
